e \/ mind<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: trust \/ approach \/ welcome<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"beware","study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":9,"ease_factor":235,"repetitions":3,"lapses":0,"learning_step":0,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-05-07","reviewed_on":"2026-05-31","due_at":"2026-06-09T21:17:20+00:00","previous_state":{"state":"review","due_at":"2026-05-31T08:55:51+00:00","interval":5,"ease_factor":235,"repetitions":2,"lapses":0,"learning_step":0,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-05-07","reviewed_on":"2026-05-26"}},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"11 nap","good":"17 nap","easy":"22 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-06-13T19:53:03+00:00"},{"id":51339,"front":"<p>After hearing the devastating news, she was completely _______ and unable to speak. <em>(feld\u00falt \/ k\u00e9ts\u00e9gbeesett)<\/em><\/p><p>The witness, still _______ from the traumatic event, struggled to recount the details to the police. <em>(zaklatott \/ felkavart)<\/em><\/p><p>He appeared _______ and disheveled, clearly having spent a sleepless night worrying about the outcome. <em>(gy\u00f6t\u00f6rt \/ megviselt)<\/em><\/p><p>The author vividly described the character&#039;s _______ state of mind, reflecting the profound grief she felt. <em>(k\u00e9ts\u00e9gbeesett \/ \u00f6sszet\u00f6rt)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">feld\u00falt \/ zaklatott \/ k\u00e9ts\u00e9gbeesett<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): nyugodt \/ kiegyens\u00falyozott \/ higgyedt<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 completely _______ = teljesen feld\u00falt (pl. She was completely _______ after the argument.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 look _______ = feld\u00faltnak t\u0171nik (pl. He looked _______ when he arrived.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 feel _______ = feld\u00faltnak \u00e9rzi ma